{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything","id":357795,"title":"Hunters and the Theory of Everything","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-02T15:22:58-08:00","id":357795,"title":"Hunters and the Theory of Everything","content":"Alright, I've seen around the place that Hunters don't play nice with the metaphysics of other lines, and egregiously so. So it has become my head-canon that <i>this is literally so</i>.<br /> <br /> Here goes:<br /> <br /> All mortals have a sort of &quot;stubbornness field&quot;; it's what lets them spend Willpower and what supplies general organizational functioning. Basically, humans got <i>inertia</i>. It's also why Supernaturals weren't responsible for any of the really big events in human history; it would be like an ant trying to deflect a bowling ball right before it hits the pin.<br /> <br /> And the Vigil amplifies this field; the sheer level of &quot;Fuck Monsters&quot; present in a Hunter cells brings it to noticeable levels.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't try any harder!&quot; &quot;FUCK YOU, RISKING WILLPOWER!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't remember anything thanks to the Sleeping Curse/Lunacy/Quiescence/whatever.&quot; &quot;FUCK YOU, I'MMA REMEMBER ANYWAY!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Um, you can't just graft stuff onto a human body and expect it to work.&quot; &quot;FUCK YOU, THAUMATECHNOLOGY!&quot;<br /> <br /> Rites of Denial already kinda work like this (&quot;Oh, you <i>aren't</i> repelled by garlic? FUCK YOU, YOU ARE NOW!&quot;) And it does help explain why Tactics are exclusive to Hunters (no-one else is able to muster the required levels of SCREW YOU I GOT MINE to make them work.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T15:59:51-08:00","id":357838,"title":"","content":"I LIKE this theory!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T02:02:46-08:00","id":358154,"title":"","content":"I come from idea that, unconsciously, humans - and by this, hunters - are stirred by God Machine to work to support the complex system as World of Darkness universe is now. Literally, Hunters works unknowingly for God Machine to take care of &quot;Secrecy Breaches&quot; that monsters from time to time do. It's lower cost effective than sending angel every time and helps to mask the existence of occult world God Machine explores. The GM only need to tweak a bit memory of those lunat,,, heroes, and it's got free agents doing it's work, without building special Infrastructures to take care of &quot;problems&quot; from time to time.<br /> <br /> It's even basic of my near coming <b>Hunter </b>game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T04:57:27-08:00","id":358202,"title":"","content":"I had a working theory for a while (even tried to make a story out of it, couldn't make it coalesce into something workable) that humans have a kind of vital spark that supernaturals lack. This manifests that, while vampires/mages/werewolves (well, maybe not werewolves... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) have the <i>power</i>, for some reason things don't really <i>change</i>. A vampire can try to his little dead hearts content to corrupt a city, but really all he's doing is jumping on and encouraging the pre-existing corruption: the static nature of vampires means they have difficulty really grasping change, let alone causing it in any meaningful sense. Werewolves can try to manipulate the spirit world, but humanities choices just seem to matter way more than spiritual urging. Plus, werewolves have enough time just keeping the screwed-up nature of the Shadow in check, let alone actually pushing it in a direction they want. Mages may have mystical knowledge, but there's always a mage countering whatever he does, because mages are contrary to each other just by nature.<br /> <br /> This is why the semi-humans of each group is so important. Ghouls, while they've been corrupted by Vitae and the lifestyle of vampires, retain choice and that vital spark, however dimmed or deluded they may be. Wolf-blooded can be, in theory, helpful to werewolves due to their walking humanities path, which werewolves can never truly do, at least after the First Change. Sleepwalkers may be aware of magic, but they're still fundamentally human, with limitations attached, which means they see things mages, blinded by their magic, cannot.<br /> <br /> *shrug* Just an idea I liked. Couldn't make it work in any meaningful sense, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T06:56:35-08:00","id":358288,"title":"","content":"Yes, I love hunter the vigil but it's a nightmare to integrate it with the other lines, I mean let's just think for a moment about the power of the conspiracies and compacts and how many there are. Let's imagine that all the compacts and conspiracies of the main book and supplements exist plus a dozen extra or more because the books heavily implies that all major countries and governments have compacts and conspiracies of their own. That's a ridiculously amount of people hunting supernatural creatures, some of them with some serious supernatural power of their own. If this was true then all supernatural creatures would behave like the changelings or demons, constantly paranoid of being captured or killed. Because taking into account how powerful some of the organizations are if they wanted they could easily wipe out all supernatural presence from a city. You have to do some major tweaks to the world in order to fit them. This is what I have done:<br /> 1-The population of supernatural creatures is high.<br /> 2-Supernatural creatures cooperate and help each other when it comes to survival.<br /> 3-Supernatural creatures have secret refuges in cities where they can gather. It can be a club, an abandoned neighborhood or an underground market. Here they exchange information, goods and favors.<br /> 4-Hunter organizations are reactionary mostly, they hunt and investigate the supernatural when it happens but rarely go beyond that.<br /> 5-Hunter organizations mostly act as pest control, killing or capturing the weakest members of the supernatural community.<br /> 6-when dealing with a very powerful supernatural opponent hunter organizations prefer to negotiate and reach some middle ground rather than all out war.<br /> What do you think?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 01-03-2015, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T18:12:19-08:00","id":358684,"title":"","content":"Hunters aren't that scary.<br /> <br /> According to the book, conspiracies have about 1000 agents each, there are about 12 conspiracies, so in todays population of almost 7 billion that makes tier three hunters less than .0002% of the population. <br /> <br /> Even throwing in the compacts, who have 50 to 200 members each, most if not all individuals types of supernaturals outnumber all organized hunters put together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T18:23:44-08:00","id":358687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=358684#post358684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hunters aren't that scary.<br /> <br /> According to the book, conspiracies have about 1000 agents each, there are about 12 conspiracies, so in todays population of almost 7 billion that makes tier three hunters less than .0002% of the population.<br /> <br /> Even throwing in the compacts, who have 50 to 200 members each, most if not all individuals types of supernaturals outnumber all organized hunters put together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how active the supernatural elements around areas are and given how self propelling the Vigil is, I wouldn't be surprised if the number of compacts that have existed in the past outnumber the supernatural organizations listed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T18:44:46-08:00","id":358695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything#post357795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I've seen around the place that Hunters don't play nice with the metaphysics of other lines, and egregiously so. So it has become my head-canon that <i>this is literally so</i>.<br /> <br /> Here goes:<br /> <br /> All mortals have a sort of &quot;stubbornness field&quot;; it's what lets them spend Willpower and what supplies general organizational functioning. Basically, humans got <i>inertia</i>. It's also why Supernaturals weren't responsible for any of the really big events in human history; it would be like an ant trying to deflect a bowling ball right before it hits the pin.<br /> <br /> And the Vigil amplifies this field; the sheer level of &quot;Fuck Monsters&quot; present in a Hunter cells brings it to noticeable levels.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't try any harder!&quot; &quot;FUCK YOU, RISKING WILLPOWER!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't remember anything thanks to the Sleeping Curse/Lunacy/Quiescence/whatever.&quot; &quot;FUCK YOU, I'MMA REMEMBER ANYWAY!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Um, you can't just graft stuff onto a human body and expect it to work.&quot; &quot;FUCK YOU, THAUMATECHNOLOGY!&quot;<br /> <br /> Rites of Denial already kinda work like this (&quot;Oh, you <i>aren't</i> repelled by garlic? FUCK YOU, YOU ARE NOW!&quot;) And it does help explain why Tactics are exclusive to Hunters (no-one else is able to muster the required levels of SCREW YOU I GOT MINE to make them work.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a word for this.<br /> <br /> Desperation.<br /> <br /> It is the most potent of human emotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T12:40:41-08:00","id":360456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=358695#post358695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a word for this.<br /> <br /> Desperation.<br /> <br /> It is the most potent of human emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, good point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T17:45:01-08:00","id":360789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=358695#post358695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a word for this.<br /> <br /> Desperation.<br /> <br /> It is the most potent of human emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I'd say anger was the most potent. Short-lived, usually, but during that time people can and do do anything, even stuff they wouldn't normally be physically capable of, adrenaline being what it is and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T18:35:35-08:00","id":360814,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no. In that sense, anger's just a dressed up and narrow version of desperation.<br /> <br /> Desperation draws on the pure power of anger, desire, despair, and fear, and just flat out does more than love, hope, or despair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T21:59:43-08:00","id":360978,"title":"","content":"Nah, desperation comes when people are backed into a corner. Anger comes when our will is thwarted or someone offends us.<br /> <br /> Agree to disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T14:33:44-08:00","id":361603,"title":"","content":"I would say our strongest trait is not Desperation but Denial. We Deny with such stubbornness &amp; arrogance that can be both positive &amp; negative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T20:03:47-08:00","id":361996,"title":"","content":"Denial isn't an emotion, per se.<br /> <br /> And if Denial really were our strongest point, humanity would never progress. Desperation grasps where denial lets slip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T21:13:48-08:00","id":362065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=361996#post361996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Denial isn't an emotion, per se.<br /> <br /> And if Denial really were our strongest point, humanity would never progress. Desperation grasps where denial lets slip.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Because we dare to dream better. We deny the limitations set to us. We were born to walk the earth, yet we deny those limits &amp; created wings to fly. Every human achievement has been in denial of limits. We are stubborn creatures against entropy &amp; when the Earth burns we will deny our extinction &amp; continue on.<br /> <br /> Most of myths &amp; heroes &amp; stories are about denial, about standing up against something, about being the underdog etc.<br /> <br /> Maybe &quot;denial&quot; isn't the right word for it. There is probably a more coherent word, but I can't think of it off the top of my head. Desperation is only one form of denial. Fighting to impose your own beliefs on the world whether that be your victory in a fight or your survival for food. It is because you deny what is happening to you with every fiber of your being. You say denial is about slipping away but you are only seeing it in its negative aspect. Denial pushes you &amp; sets you free, whether that is good or bad. It is an arrogant emotion but it lets us harness lightning &amp; even come back from death only because we will it.<br /> <br /> &amp; That is why humans can risk Willpower. Every other creature is fighting something inherent.<br /> A vampire is fighting it's beast<br /> A werewolf is fighting it's dual nature<br /> A geist is fighting it's spirit<br /> A mage is fighting the lie<br /> <br /> A hunter, a human, is fighting the world, &amp; as time has proven, the world loses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T21:40:05-08:00","id":362083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aermas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=362065#post362065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Because we dare to dream better. We deny the limitations set to us. We were born to walk the earth, yet we deny those limits &amp; created wings to fly. Every human achievement has been in denial of limits. We are stubborn creatures against entropy &amp; when the Earth burns we will deny our extinction &amp; continue on.<br /> <br /> Most of myths &amp; heroes &amp; stories are about denial, about standing up against something, about being the underdog etc.<br /> <br /> Maybe &quot;denial&quot; isn't the right word for it. There is probably a more coherent word, but I can't think of it off the top of my head. Desperation is only one form of denial. Fighting to impose your own beliefs on the world whether that be your victory in a fight or your survival for food. It is because you deny what is happening to you with every fiber of your being. You say denial is about slipping away but you are only seeing it in its negative aspect. Denial pushes you &amp; sets you free, whether that is good or bad. It is an arrogant emotion but it lets us harness lightning &amp; even come back from death only because we will it.<br /> <br /> &amp; That is why humans can risk Willpower. Every other creature is fighting something inherent.<br /> A vampire is fighting it's beast<br /> A werewolf is fighting it's dual nature<br /> A geist is fighting it's spirit<br /> A mage is fighting the lie<br /> <br /> A hunter, a human, is fighting the world, &amp; as time has proven, the world loses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Defiance sounds like the word you're looking for. I think in this situation the difference between Defiance and Desperation is more academic than not. Defiance is born out of desperation, because if we weren't desperate, we wouldn't need to defy things in the first place, or whatever. It's really not that simple, but for the purposes of the discussion I don't really think what you're suggesting is really all that different from this idea of desperation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T21:44:38-08:00","id":362089,"title":"","content":"Defiance is angry desperation.<br /> <br /> Denial isn't really an emotion so much as it is an emotion. I have felt defiance, and I have been in denial, but I've never felt denial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T21:53:06-08:00","id":362094,"title":"","content":"You know, if we replace the word &quot;desperation&quot; with &quot;passion&quot;, it works a lot better.<br /> <br /> Desperation is attached to passion, to be sure, but I wouldn't say they're the same thing. But, it does work with the formulation better. Anger is passionate, defiance is borne of passion, and passion drives humans to kick reality in the face and change it in such a way that no other species can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T07:59:51-08:00","id":362439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=362094#post362094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, if we replace the word &quot;desperation&quot; with &quot;passion&quot;, it works a lot better.<br /> <br /> Desperation is attached to passion, to be sure, but I wouldn't say they're the same thing. But, it does work with the formulation better. Anger is passionate, defiance is borne of passion, and passion drives humans to kick reality in the face and change it in such a way that no other species can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the way you understand the relationship. I don't agree with the argument, but that comes from the way I've experienced both emotions and what I've gotten from it, and can see what you're saying.<br /> <br /> ...But I will say that between the two, Desperation sounds better for the World of Darkness, and has already been highlighted a few times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T09:03:37-08:00","id":362509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheArchitect</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I thought werewolves had anger issues.<br /> <br /> I like your version of Hunters. They're like a nest of ants after you lace their food source with steroids.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I can see Hunters doing, if they had enough resources.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://fc00.deviantart.net/fs70/f/2010/001/9/9/Hell_Yeah_by_Gannadene.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With <i>strong</i> under-and-overtones of<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xCENkwPiuU0\" data-code=\"xCENkwPiuU0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/xCENkwPiuU0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T13:57:13-08:00","id":362849,"title":"","content":"I don't think it works particularly well. It replaces Hunters fighting with ingenuity and sheer audacity with Hunters being secretly magic. It forces Hunters to be portrayed in a very narrow fashion, as well as simply removing any intrigue from the endowments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T14:03:14-08:00","id":362858,"title":"","content":"To be honest... I disagree with you Michael.<br /> <br /> This <i>is</i> sheer audacity; it's &quot;secretly magical&quot; in the way that adrenaline and craptons of research are magical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T15:00:48-08:00","id":362920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This <i>is</i> sheer audacity; it's &quot;secretly magical&quot; in the way that adrenaline and craptons of research are magical. </div> </div> </div>I meant it in a more narrative sense. You're building a normal human activity into some kind of metaphysical power. Normal audacity would be pretending to be a good victim for a vampire and then when one attacks you, shooting them in the face, hoping that the sheer surprise will carry you through. It's a description of the way someone acts, it's not a power source that lets you alter the universe.<br /> <br /> I guess you could do something with that, I mean it sounds a lot like Pyros, which could be cool. But it still removes a lot from Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T15:17:48-08:00","id":362950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=362849#post362849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it works particularly well. It replaces Hunters fighting with ingenuity and sheer audacity with Hunters being secretly magic. It forces Hunters to be portrayed in a very narrow fashion, as well as simply removing any intrigue from the endowments.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it makes me wonder if we've secretly moved out of nWoD's area of secret but discoverable truths in favor of oWoD's of reality is what you make of it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T15:59:19-08:00","id":362988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=362920#post362920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a description of the way someone acts, it's not a power source that lets you alter the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't it be both? To quote misremembered poetry, <i>Alone, godless, an injured cat cures itself with its tongue.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T16:13:01-08:00","id":362994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=362988#post362988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why can't it be both? To quote misremembered poetry, <i>Alone, godless, an injured cat cures itself with its tongue.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>In a sense, it already is \u2014 inasmuch as it already is a power source that lets you alter the universe in real life. That is to say, metaphorically so. It lets you alter the universe in that being audacious sets you free to achieve effects nobody anticipated you could achieve, not even yourself. That's the level on which audacity is a power source in Hunter: the Vigil, the level that risking Willpower represents. It's not a metaphysical force.<br /> <br /> As to why it can't also be a metaphysical force? Sure it can, it's fiction, and if you enjoy that at your table, go for it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't expect anybody to consider it an inbuilt feature of Hunter: the Vigil, though, because making this literal statement about the nWoD universe in turn makes an <i>artistic</i> statement about the nWoD that isn't to the thrust of the gamelines' themes. It says that &quot;rah rah, fight the power&quot; is a tangible energy, that you can achieve anything if you put your mind to it, and that the game is <i>about</i> that to the degree that it has rules and in-setting energies to enforce it. I'm all about affording mortal hunters all kinds of impact and agency through their grit and organization and everything they've sacrificed, but the horror atmosphere of Hunter in specific and the nWoD in general rests on the cornerstone that nothing is certain. That means, among other things, that sometimes good people give it everything they've got without holding back and fail.<br /> <br /> Once you're making artistic statements that connote against this, you're shifting the genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T17:03:50-08:00","id":363034,"title":"","content":"True enough; I did mean it more in the metaphorical sense (with the understanding that metaphors can sometimes have teeth.)<br /> <br /> And it's actually pretty in genre to have desperation, denial, SCIENCE, and sheer bloody-mindedness do impossible (and horrifying) things. After all, remember that Lovecraft had men of science hunting Vampires with a laser gun <i>way</i> before it was cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T19:03:05-08:00","id":363122,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm not a fan of the conspiracies. I find they tend to shift the tone of a game too far from the 'fighting the darkness alone or near-alone because it's <i>the right thing to do'</i>. I'm not going to say they're unworkable, because it depends on the group/game/etc, but if I were to use them, it'd be in the form of something like:<br /> <br /> A member of the cell got ripped up pretty bad in that last run at the wolf-people on the hill, too bad for the vet to patch up. So they had to drop him at the ER and spin a story about how they found him torn up on the side of the road. The other members of the cell can't hang around too much or it'd draw suspicion (and more suspicion is the last thing they need after that house fire last month, what with their car being seen fleeing the scene), but they spend as much time as they can afford to keep an eye out.<br /> <br /> One day, the ripped-up member, let's call him Jim, disappears. Talking to the nursing staff indicates that he was transferred to another hospital to get specialist attention; checking on the hospital reveals it's bogus. The cell scrambles, trying their best to track Jim down, even hacking the hospital security recordings and getting an ambulance with a fake license plate. Just as the cell is fearing the worst, Jim returns to the first hospital, seeming no worse for wear. He remembers nothing of his time away, but seems to have been well taken care of. However, a few weeks later, in the middle of a desperate fight with the wolf-people who put Jim in the hospital the first time, Jims arm suddenly grows to double its length, his fingers tipped with vicious claws that tear hunks of flesh out of the wolves hides. It reverts after the wolves retreat, but the cell is left asking... <i>what the hell?!</i><br /> <br /> Something like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=362439#post362439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the way you understand the relationship. I don't agree with the argument, but that comes from the way I've experienced both emotions and what I've gotten from it, and can see what you're saying.<br /> <br /> ...But I will say that between the two, Desperation sounds better for the World of Darkness, and has already been highlighted a few times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. I don't agree, but I can appreciate your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=363034#post363034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True enough; I did mean it more in the metaphorical sense (with the understanding that metaphors can sometimes have teeth.)<br /> <br /> And it's actually pretty in genre to have desperation, denial, SCIENCE, and sheer bloody-mindedness do impossible (and horrifying) things. After all, remember that Lovecraft had men of science hunting Vampires with a laser gun <i>way</i> before it was cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovecraft had laser guns? I've read some of his work, and I missed that part (that said, I tend to favour his short stories rather than his full-length novel stuff, so not surprising).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T19:26:17-08:00","id":363133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=363122#post363122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm not a fan of the conspiracies. I find they tend to shift the tone of a game too far from the 'fighting the darkness alone or near-alone because it's <i>the right thing to do'</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it though?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T19:29:35-08:00","id":363136,"title":"","content":"Hunters think so. Course, hunters aren't exactly the most stable of individuals, so take that with a grain of salt","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T19:34:55-08:00","id":363142,"title":"","content":"Dude, look up &quot;The Shunned House&quot;; it might not be <i>actual</i> lasers, and it might not have <i>actually</i> worked, but yep, they gave it a try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T19:49:37-08:00","id":363151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=363136#post363136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters think so. Course, hunters aren't exactly the most stable of individuals, so take that with a grain of salt</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the grains of salt find their home in the conspiracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T20:08:18-08:00","id":363159,"title":"","content":"Sure, but receiving a paycheck for it kind-of legitimises it (not really, but hopefully you get what I'm grasping for): it's not something done out of obsession or passion or gut-feel that these things are <i>wrong</i>, but because it's your job, or because the Conspiracy will kill you if you don't. Even the sample descriptions of the people in the Conspiracies describe people just kind of falling into it rather than choosing or being driven to the Vigil. Like I said, they're not bad or unworkable, just different, and not what I like about Hunter games.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, they're often mysterious and ambiguous and such, but it's somehow a different kind of horror? I mean, if we accept vampires and that as wrong, which seems to be the default view of Hunter (although any specific hunter may and probably does vary depending on their specific perspective), then Aegis Kai Doru collecting magic relics for their own purposes is more an ambiguous, I-think-this-is-right-as-far-as-I-can-tell worry. Cheiron I never really found horrific at all; the body horror I guess, but they're more just kind of amoral than actually malevolent. The implications of being controlled by Cthulhu aside, they do want to help protect people, if nothing else because it doesn't help their bottom line (and if they're going for Umbrella-type thing, I always thought that was just silly rather than actually believable). Stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T20:19:34-08:00","id":363166,"title":"","content":"You make it sound like Cainites get paid and Division Six don't, which is kind of backwards. I'd say most of the Conspiracies don't get paid for it. Course, most of the Compacts don't either.<br /> <br /> I find the Compacts to be the natural reaction of people to the darkness when allowed to go on en masse, but Conspiracies are where the dirty questions come up, as well as the truly hopeful ideals fight to grow. It's where the human/monster dichotomy (mostly) breaks down and some serious questions about what we're actually trying to do comes up, with the vague hope that maybe we can transcend the circumstances and make a world where we can all live together comfortably regardless of humanity or monstrosity sitting somewhere in the middle of all of that.<br /> <br /> Certain people don't like the Conspiracies because it quite often seems like monsters are pulling the strings, and that's true, but it also creates an interesting situation where human and monster work together. Some are in bad company, like the Knights of both Saint George and Saint Adrian, but the principle is still really hopeful-if you believe you can work through the vast thorny maze that precedes it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T20:35:03-08:00","id":363173,"title":"","content":"I'm not touching the extra books; I've leafed through them, but generally I find they don't really add much in my games. And a lot of them don't get paid, but then they tend to be the ones that brainwash their Hunters like the Lucifuge or Aegis Kai Doru (so presumably the characters, as members, are also brainwashed, so they're not going to be asking questions), or are more 'moderate', like the Ascending Ones, which is again a different kind of game. Or you don't have a real choice, like Cheiron or TFV, because they'll kill you if you don't (and Cheiron or TFV are either amoral or more-or-less in favour of helping people, respectively. Yeah, they're inefficient as all get-out, and maybe there's something there, but large organisations tend to be inefficient anyway, as anyone who's worked in government or large corporations is well aware, without needing any corruption).<br /> <br /> Compacts are fine, since they pretty much just share info, and that info is unreliable at best. They are a different type of game again, but close enough to Tier 1 games that it's still workable for me. But conspiracies? Too far removed from the original for my taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T20:48:13-08:00","id":363179,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I'm not partial to the....'blindness' that tends to accompany the lower tiers, but there's no reason for that to be a thing-hell, there's a reason tier one is my favorite after tier three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T01:58:44-08:00","id":363284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=363173#post363173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (and Cheiron or TFV are either amoral or more-or-less in favour of helping people, respectively. Yeah, they're inefficient as all get-out, and maybe there's something there, but large organisations tend to be inefficient anyway, as anyone who's worked in government or large corporations is well aware, without needing any corruption).</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue isn't so much monstrosity in and of it's self but rather the source of it. There is a much different tone in saying Cheiron's Board of Directors are external aliens vs a host of Really REALLY old hunters who learned about Thaumatechnology when Rome was a major player in the world and have been hunting monsters to keep their decaying bodies alive (Oh and to make a few bucks here and there with the added bonus of making the world a better place).<br /> <br /> Even the Vampires in TFV trope can be turned completely on it's head by having Abe at the helm of it because it gives well need grey-area legitimacy and justification. A vampire is in charge but the person is a former president.<br /> <br /> I personally find the trope of &quot;Compromised organization&quot; somewhat simplistic and occasionally tiresome. It's much more interesting when the trope is subverted in more than a few ways. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T07:30:18-08:00","id":363476,"title":"","content":"I find the idea that the Conspiracies aren't in-genre a little bizarre though I understand your perspectives, I think they focus on only one aspect of the mentioned conspiracies themselves.<br /> <br /> Spin, spin, spin.<br /> <br /> The Malleus can't be anymore the epitome of classic hunter, after all, they -are- the Exorcist or Bugenhagen from Omen. They're the experts on the &quot;devil&quot; and his agents on Earth! They're not only doing it because it is the right thing to do but because it is the -righteous- thing to do. While you can look from the corrupt perspectives of those controlling these organizations, player character hunters are going to be the men on the ground and for them it will likely be the mission statement. You're going to probably be Father Merrin or Bugenhagen more than the Pope or the Cardinals.<br /> <br /> Aegis also struck me as while carrying plenty of room as greedy and corrupt individuals, they're a bit like the Library, from those be movies from the mid-2000's. (Though a little darker in tone.) They hunt monsters and acquire their artefacts so that they can be used to help people rather than hurt in the hands of the monsters.<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge and Cheiron are for those players who want to play the Hellboy trope a little. They want to blur the line of what it means to be a Hunter and the thing that you hunt. I feel like these two conspiracies would be more hidden than the others, especially their agenda, and especially from their boots on the ground. For the Lucifuge it's a 'family that took me in' after some Malleus guy tried to kill me claiming me the antichrist, while the Cheiron group might be more &quot;You did good out there today, bill. Shame about the leg. Listen, there's some... experimental surgery the boffins down in R&amp;D have been pushing. ...just... sign here, wouldja?&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel like all of these conspiracies are well within genre. Perhaps Lucifuge and Cheiron are more for those Hunters who falter on their path up the tiers but I think Malleus and Aegis are definately easy to see as 'good guys against the dark'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T17:47:47-08:00","id":363947,"title":"","content":"The conspiracies are essentially the epitome of the dark mystery described in the World of Darkness core book than most splats have gotten. They turn a standard game of hack and slash into a World of Darkness hunter game.<br /> <br /> Not liking vampires running Task Force Valkyrie or other conspiracies being influenced by dark forces is more of an out of character preference. 'I like Task Force Valkyrie. I don't like that they're controlled by vampires.' <br /> <br /> From a gaming standpoint, it's great, because it allows you to play a hunter while also uncovering the dark mysteries of the World of Darkness. And a quote from the core, 'The world is one of shadows within shadows. Those who participate in these conspiracies should uncover as much of them as they can, lest investigators become unwitting pawns in the games of greater forces. But drawing back the curtain on one mystery reveals even more curtains, each hiding new secrets. It's not possible to uncover them all. Yet, characters can certainly work to reveal more than would otherwise be known, and so free themselves from these dark influences.'<br /> <br /> Your character doesn't know that they're being manipulated by vampires, or being used as a pawn in a struggle for control of a conspiracy by two opposing forces. But they have the opportunity to find out, and create more story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T19:41:06-08:00","id":364029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=363476#post363476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the idea that the Conspiracies aren't in-genre a little bizarre though I understand your perspectives, I think they focus on only one aspect of the mentioned conspiracies themselves.<br /> <br /> Spin, spin, spin.<br /> <br /> The Malleus can't be anymore the epitome of classic hunter, after all, they -are- the Exorcist or Bugenhagen from Omen. They're the experts on the &quot;devil&quot; and his agents on Earth! They're not only doing it because it is the right thing to do but because it is the -righteous- thing to do. While you can look from the corrupt perspectives of those controlling these organizations, player character hunters are going to be the men on the ground and for them it will likely be the mission statement. You're going to probably be Father Merrin or Bugenhagen more than the Pope or the Cardinals.<br /> <br /> Aegis also struck me as while carrying plenty of room as greedy and corrupt individuals, they're a bit like the Library, from those be movies from the mid-2000's. (Though a little darker in tone.) They hunt monsters and acquire their artefacts so that they can be used to help people rather than hurt in the hands of the monsters.<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge and Cheiron are for those players who want to play the Hellboy trope a little. They want to blur the line of what it means to be a Hunter and the thing that you hunt. I feel like these two conspiracies would be more hidden than the others, especially their agenda, and especially from their boots on the ground. For the Lucifuge it's a 'family that took me in' after some Malleus guy tried to kill me claiming me the antichrist, while the Cheiron group might be more &quot;You did good out there today, bill. Shame about the leg. Listen, there's some... experimental surgery the boffins down in R&amp;D have been pushing. ...just... sign here, wouldja?&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel like all of these conspiracies are well within genre. Perhaps Lucifuge and Cheiron are more for those Hunters who falter on their path up the tiers but I think Malleus and Aegis are definately easy to see as 'good guys against the dark'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I get it, it <i>can</i> be lots of fun. But it's a different kind of game. If you're a more-or-less regular Joe who is fighting to protect his family from the bloodsuckers who are in the neighborhood, that's one kind of game. If you have an organisation giving you UV bullets (yeah, I know it doesn't work like that, hush) or new limbs, it's a totally different type of game. There's near-no chance that you're just a whackadoo, which is a big part of Hunter as I see it (the irony being that they are both crazy <i>and</i> right <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). If you're a priest fighting back the forces of the Devil under the nose of everyone, walking a dark path to protect the parishoners, even with a small group of faithful, that's one type of game. If you've got a multinational group backing you, that inherently changes the game.<br /> <br /> Neither are <i>bad</i>. Just different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T07:23:01-08:00","id":368595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/357795-hunters-and-the-theory-of-everything?p=363284#post363284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally find the trope of &quot;Compromised organization&quot; somewhat simplistic and occasionally tiresome. It's much more interesting when the trope is subverted in more than a few ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I kind of like the notion that lower tier members of an organization don't really realize how deeply in bed their group has been with others in the past; it can lead to astonishingly short sighted and frustrating decision making of the type that can spawn whole conflicts by itself.<br /> <br /> That being said, it does feel like, at times, there is subversion for subversion's sake. Nowhere, I think, is that more evident than a group named &quot;The Hammer of Witches&quot; being described as primarily focused on hunting vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T07:31:49-08:00","id":368599,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind there's an entire covenant of vampire witches, and before Witchfinders, no other witches in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T07:56:09-08:00","id":368613,"title":"","content":"Eh... I would disagree; even if the original Hunter book came out before Mage or Second Sight (it came out three and two years after, respectively), it has buckets of Dread Powers that you could use to devise magicians with. More to the point, there's other groups in Hunter whose primary target is magicians (and others whose primary target is vampires) and it feels odd that the Malleus isn't one of them. The Malleus Maleficarum feels like it should be fighting demons and witches first and foremost on the name alone, but behind that is also the history of the Inquisition and the very nature of the holy book they use in their worship that states &quot;maleficos non patieris vivere&quot;. Their chapter fiction is all about them fighting demons. It makes the whole &quot;Their primary target is vampires&quot; bit feel... Silly.<br /> <br /> The Malleus, to me, is sort of an opportunity to have fun with a grand, slightly dogmatic conspiracy where questions of faith brush against a reality that does not give easy answers, and where the compassionate heroes of one week are very easily the bigoted villains of the next. Maybe that's treading too much on the Long Night's territory, I don't know, but the secret vampire-eating conspiracy bit feels out of place with an organization like that. I could understand if there was a heretical schism, say, where one group wanted to bind demons to use against the devil's purposes, or perhaps claims that the angels that sometimes provide aid/assistance to the Malleus seem... Strange, somehow; these would feel like natural internal troubles for such an organization to have. The vampire bit just feels strange.<br /> <br /> Your mileage may vary, this is just my feelings on the matter. In any game I run, that's how I focus them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T17:13:13-08:00","id":369177,"title":"","content":"I love conspiracies for one simple reason, the tension that comes working for them. Imagine that the players are happy and loyal hunters of one of the conspiracies and then little by little you start introducing things that make them doubt. Suddenly their friendly handler doesn't look so trustworthy anymore, they start to question why some objectives are chosen over others and they wonder where really do their endowments come from. My point is the potential for paranoia and tension is endless, never knowing who to trust or who you can rely on. Not only they have to worry about what are they hunting, they also have to watch their backs less their supposed benefactors betray them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}